{"repositoryId":1379510757,"availability":"available","full":"Tom-Brenner/genmol-editing-policy","name":"genmol-editing-policy","description":"Learning edit-site selection for frozen GenMol remasking: LightGBM-guided constrained QED improvement on ChEMBL. Preprint: https://chemrxiv.org/doi/full/10.26434/chemrxiv.15010340/v2 · Demo: https://huggingface.co/spaces/one-more-beauty/genmol-edit-site-policy","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T10:25:19Z","updated":"2026-10-14T15:39:28Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["chembl","cheminformatics","computational-chemistry","drug-discovery","gradio","huggingface-spaces","lightgbm","machine-learning","molecular-generation","molecular-optimization","rdkit"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/one-more-beauty/genmol-edit-site-policy","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.729Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.729Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.729Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.729Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repository evaluates policies that select one eligible peripheral fragment to remask with frozen GenMol V1 (Lee et al., ICML 2025). The selected edit must preserve the Bemis–Murcko core and satisfy similarity, size, validity, and QED-improvement constraints. The learned LightGBM policy is compared with random and largest-fragment baselines on a core-disjoint ChEMBL holdout.","The demo scores eligible cut sites; it does not generate molecules or make claims about potency, safety, or synthesis."],"features":["Interactive Hugging Face demo"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Tom-Brenner/genmol-editing-policy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4599b12a9886a6755c6e1b35ca00bfccea3e2b3b7a5209b10f0bf637bdfeb6c7","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.873Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:04.873Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItD